s=para(s,'Records were retained when',r'''Records were retained when they reported measurements from sensory afferents, investigated feedback in locomotion or posture, or modeled a sensory pathway relevant to those tasks. Here, a sensory pathway means the route by which a sensory signal influences neural activity or motor output, such as force feedback from a muscle influencing the transition from stance to swing. Reviews helped organize the subject and locate primary evidence. Duplicate records and material outside this scope were archived. Classification used a consistent set of tags for the experimental preparation and afferent class, allowing papers that used different terminology to be retrieved together. Each mechanism summary was based on the available source text, using the abstract when full text was unavailable.''',n,'M-082/083: define sensory pathway and replace unexplained controlled-vocabulary terminology.')
