old='Second, the project lacked validated neuromechanical models linking a spinal CPG to both a human-scale musculoskeletal model and its BPA-routed robot counterpart.'
new='Second, the project lacked a tested framework for connecting neural controllers to its human musculoskeletal reference and BPA-actuated models, with control over mechanical support, sensory inputs, and disturbances.'
assert old in s;changes.append(dict(file=n,reason='Align the opening gap with the implemented framework rather than implying complete model validation.',before=old,after=new));s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=E/'chapters/70-overall.tex';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');n=p.name
s=para(s,'The fourth enabler is',r'''The fourth enabler is the neuromechanical simulation framework (Chapter~\ref{ch:sns}). It connects OpenSim-derived mechanics to neural controllers, evaluates BPA forces within coupled models, and provides graphical circuit construction and matched implementation tests. Adjustable support, staged parameter tuning, neural stimuli, pathway removal, and mechanical perturbations make controller behavior testable under specified conditions. The demonstrated results include agreement of the contact-driven rhythm core across implementations, BPA-actuated air stepping and supported standing, and W2L pathway tests. The latter identify Ib dependence at one operating point while also exposing posture failures under mechanical perturbation. No harness-free walking has been demonstrated. In separate hardware work, a BPA-actuated limb maintained balance using pseudo-vestibular inertial feedback \citep{bolen_balance_2024, bolen_selfbalancing_2024, bolen_selfbalancing_srs_2024}. Extending these components to unsupported bilateral walking, wider model transfer, and embedded execution remains future work.''',n,'Align the synthesis with current demonstrated capabilities and corrected result scope; avoid a novelty inventory.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=E/'chapters/80-conclusion.tex';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');n=p.name
s=para(s,'The sensory-afferent resource of',r'''The sensory-afferent resource of Chapter~\ref{ch:database} makes relevant physiological reports easier to locate and compare while retaining their experimental context. Chapter~\ref{ch:sns} provides a framework for connecting neural controllers to mechanical models and testing them under specified support, stimulation, and perturbation conditions. Independent implementations reproduced the contact-driven rhythm core with exact period agreement and trace correlations above 0.9999. BPA-actuated models demonstrated air stepping and supported standing. The coupled pathway and perturbation tests identified model-specific feedback dependence and posture limitations. These results establish implemented experimental capabilities; harness-free walking remains unachieved.''',n,'Replace the stale tonic-mismatch summary with current capabilities and limits.')
